// Signing for the Pops app target and its test bundle — a test bundle signed by
// nobody cannot be installed alongside a host that is, so both read this file.
// Automatic signing needs a team, and the team
// is the one part of this configuration that is not the same for everyone who
// clones a public repo — so it is read from outside the tree rather than
// committed.
//
// `Signing.local.xcconfig` is gitignored and written by `mise run generate` from
// `~/.config/pops/ios-signing.xcconfig`, which is what lets one file on the
// machine serve every clone and worktree. It has to be an indirection rather
// than an include of the home path directly: a project-referenced xcconfig
// resolves neither `~` nor `$(HOME)` in an include path, and silently includes
// nothing when it cannot resolve one.
//
// The optional form means a machine that has never set this up still builds for
// the simulator. Setup, and the error you get without it, are in ../README.md.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
